          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} Simplicial sets
            are the archetypical combinatorial “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"}> model
            ” for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            of (compactly generated weakly Hausdorff)
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29Cat"} (∞,1)Cat
            itself.
          %p
            This statement is made precise by the existence of the structure of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
            that is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presentation
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} (infinity,1)-category
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            %strong Joyal model structure
            which similarly is a presentation of the
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)Cat
          %h2#classical_model_structure Classical Model Structure
          %p
            The
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi sSet
                      %mi Quillen
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Quillen}
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  %strong cofibrations
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  are simply the
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo :
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
                  which are precisely the levelwise injections, i.e. the morphisms of simplicial sets such that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi n
                        %mo :
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi n
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi Y
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_n : X_n \to Y_n
                  is an injection of sets for all
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi ℕ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  %strong weak equivalences
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                  are
                  = succeed "," do
                    %strong weak homotopy equivalences
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
                  is a weak homotopy equivalence of topological spaces.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The
                %strong fibrations
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                are the
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibration"}> Kan fibration
                    s
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
                which have the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
                with respect to all
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horn"} horn
                inclusions.
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
