          %h3#constructive_version Constructive version
          %p
            The original
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proofs"} proofs
            of the existence of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
            are based in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mathematics"} classical mathematics
            as they use the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principle+of+excluded+middle"} principle of excluded middle
            and the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internalization
            into the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            requires
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive
            methods for interpreting
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proofs+as+programs"} proofs as programs
          %p
            A constructively valid model structure on simplicial sets and coinciding with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure
            if
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            are assumed was found in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "constructive+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets#Henry19"} Henry 19
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "constructive+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets#GambinoSattlerSzumilo19"} Gambino-Sattler-Szumiło 19
          %p
            See at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} constructive model structure on simplicial sets
          %h2#joyals_model_structure Joyal’s Model Structure
          %p
            There is a second model structure on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi sSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
            – the
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+quasi-categories"} model structure for quasi-categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi sSet
                    %mi Joyal
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Joyal}
            – which is different (not
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalent
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"} André Joyal
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrations"} cofibrations
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi sSet
                        %mi Joy
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Joy}
                are the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphisms"} monomorphisms
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injections"} injections
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalences"} weak equivalences
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi sSet
                        %mi Joy
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Joy}
                are
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+categorical+equivalences"} weak categorical equivalences
              %p
                namely those
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maps"} maps
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi u
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \colon A \rightarrow B
                of simplicial sets such that the induced map
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi u
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msup
                        %mi X
                        %mi B
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi X
                        %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u^* \colon X^B \rightarrow X^A
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+homs"} internal homs
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+complexes"}> mapping complexes
                ) for all
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-category"} quasi-categories
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                induces an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                when applying the functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi τ
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_0
                that takes a simplicial set to the set of isomorphism classes of objects of its fundamental category.
            %li
              %p
                The fibrations
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                are called variously
                %strong isofibrations
                or
                = succeed "." do
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+Kan+fibration"} quasi-fibrations
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+cofibrations"} acyclic cofibrations
                already defined.
              %p
                Quasi-fibrations between weak Kan complexes have a simple description; they are precisely the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+Kan+fibrations"} inner Kan fibrations
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horn"} horn
                inclusions and also the inclusion
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi j
                        %mn 0
                      %mo :
                      %mo *
                      %mo →
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_0 : * \rightarrow J
                where
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *
                is the terminal simplicial set and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                is the nerve of the groupoid on two objects with one non-trivial isomorphism.
          %p
            All objects are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+object"} cofibrant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+objects"} fibrant objects
            are precisely the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-categories"} quasi-categories
          %p
            This model structure is cofibrantly generated. The generating cofibrations are the set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            described above. There is no known explicit description for the generating trivial cofibrations.
          %p
            Importantly, this model structure is Quillen equivalent to several alternative model structures for the ‘’homotopy theory of homotopy theories“ such as that on the category of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicially+enriched+category"} simplicially enriched categories
          %h3#comparison Comparison
          %p
            Every weak categorical equivalence is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+weak+homotopy+equivalence"} simplicial weak homotopy equivalence
            (but not conversely). Since both model structures have the same class of cofibrations (namely the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphisms"} monomorphisms
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization"} Bousfield localization
            of
            %span.newWikiWord
              Joyal's model structure
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Joyal%27s+model+structure"} ?
            (namely at the
            = succeed "-inclusions):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/outer+horn"} outer horn
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi sSet
                    %mi KQ
                  %munderover
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ⊥
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi id
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟵
                      %mi id
                  %msub
                    %mi sSet
                    %mi Joy
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  sSet_{KQ}
                  \\underoverset
                  {\underset{id}{\longrightarrow}}
                  {\overset{id}{\longleftarrow}}
                  {\;\; \bot \;\;}
                  sSet_{Joy}
                  \\,.
          %h2#fibrant_replacement Fibrant replacement
          %p
            Fibrant replacement in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi sSet
                    %mi Quillen
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Quillen}
            models the process of
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                \-groupoidification
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-morphism"} k-morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi sSet
                    %mi Quillen
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Quillen}
            are discussed at
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibrant+replacement"}> Kan fibrant replacement
              \.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+topological+spaces"}> model structure on topological spaces
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+semi-simplicial+sets"} model structure on semi-simplicial sets
          %h2#properness Properness
          %p
            The Quillen model structure is both left and right
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+model+category"} proper
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            which (1) preserves fibrations, (2) preserves pullbacks of fibrations, (3) preserves and reflects weak equivalences, and (4) lands in a category in which the pullback of a weak equivalence along a fibration is a weak equivalence. For if so, we can apply
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            to the pullback of a fibration along a weak equivalence to get another such pullback in the codomain of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            are
          %ul
            %li
              geometric realization
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi sSet
                      %mo →
                      %mi Top
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet \to Top
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
              denotes a sufficiently
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convenient+category+of+topological+spaces"} convenient category of topological spaces
              (e.g. the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-spaces"} k-spaces
              suffices) and
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ex
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo :
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo →
                    %mi Kan
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ex^\infty : sSet \to Kan
              , where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Kan
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Kan
              is the category of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complexes"} Kan complexes
          %p
            This can be found, for instance, in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#GoerssJardine"} Goerss-Jardine, Cor. II.9.6
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Moss"} Moss
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Cisinski06"} Cisinski, Prop. 2.1.5
          %h2#references References
          %div
            %h3#classical_model_structure_on_simplicial_sets Classical model structure on simplicial sets
            %p
              On the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
            %p The original proof is due to
            %ul
              %li#Quillen67
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Quillen"}> Daniel Quillen
                , Section II.3 of:
                %em Axiomatic homotopy theory
                in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Homotopical+Algebra"} Homotopical Algebra
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0097438"} doi:10.1007/BFb0097438
            %p
              This proof is purely
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorics"} combinatorial
              (i.e. does not pass through
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
              as
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/minimal+Kan+fibrations"} minimal Kan fibrations
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundles"} fiber bundles
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+classifying+space"} simplicial classifying space
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+group"} simplicial group
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            %p Other proofs are were given in:
            %ul
              %li#GelfandManin96
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergei+Gelfand"}> Sergei Gelfand
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yuri+Manin"} Yuri Manin
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Methods+of+homological+algebra"} Methods of homological algebra
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-662-12492-5"} doi:10.1007/978-3-662-12492-5
              %li#GoerssJardine99
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Goerss"}> Paul Goerss
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+F.+Jardine"} J. F. Jardine
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simplicial+homotopy+theory"} Simplicial homotopy theory
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-0346-0189-4"} doi:10.1007/978-3-0346-0189-4
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://web.archive.org/web/19990208220238/http://www.math.uwo.ca/~jardine/papers/simp-sets/"} webpage
              %li#JoyalTierney08
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"}> André Joyal
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Myles+Tierney"} Myles Tierney
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Notes on simplicial homotopy theory
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      %a{:href => "https://lists.lehigh.edu/pipermail/algtop-l/2007q4/000017.html"} Advanced Course on Simplicial Methods in Higher Categories
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/JoyalTierneyNotesOnSimplicialHomotopyTheory.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %li#JoyalTierney09
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"}> André Joyal
                  ,
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Myles+Tierney"} Myles Tierney
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em An introduction to simplicial homotopy theory
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "http://hopf.math.purdue.edu/cgi-bin/generate?/Joyal-Tierney/JT-chap-01"} web
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/JoyalTierneySimplicialHomotopyTheory.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %p
              A proof (in fact two variants of it) using the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibrant+replacement"} Kan fibrant replacement
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ex
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ex^\infty
              functor is given (in the context of_
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cisinski+model+structure"} Cisinski model structure
              %em ) in:
            %ul
              %li#Cisinski06
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"}> Denis-Charles Cisinski
                , Section 2 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/joyalscatlab/published/Les+pr%C3%A9faisceaux+comme+type+d%27homotopie"} Les préfaisceaux comme type d'homotopie
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.univ-toulouse.fr/~dcisinsk/ast.pdf"} pdf
            %p
              The crucial step is the proof that the fibrations are precisely the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibrations"} Kan fibrations
              (and also to prove all the good properties of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ex
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ex^\infty
              without using topological spaces); for two different proofs of this fact using
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Ex
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ex^\infty
            %p
              Another approach using
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ex
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ex^\infty
              is:
            %ul
              %li#Moss
                Sean Moss,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Another approach to the Kan-Quillen model structure
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1506.04887"} arXiv:1506.04887
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s40062-019-00247-y"} doi:10.1007/s40062-019-00247-y
            %p
              A proof of the model structure not relying on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
              nor on explicit models for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibrant+replacement"} Kan fibrant replacement
              is in
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Sattler"}> Christian Sattler
                ,
                %em The Equivalence Extension Property and Model Structures
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1704.06911"}> arXiv:1704.06911
                )
            %p
              Proofs valid in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
              are given in:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simon+Henry"}> Simon Henry
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em A constructive account of the Kan-Quillen model structure and of Kan’s Ex∞ functor
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1905.06160"} arXiv:1905.06160
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicola+Gambino"}> Nicola Gambino
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simon+Henry"} Simon Henry
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Sattler"} Christian Sattler
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Karol+Szumi%C5%82o"} Karol Szumiło
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em The effective model structure and ∞-groupoid objects
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2102.06146"} arXiv:2102.06146
            %p
              As a
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "relation+between+type+theory+and+category+theory#HomotopyTypeTheory"} categorical semantics for homotopy type theory
            %ul
              %li#KapulkinLumnsdaineVoevodsky12
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Kapulkin"}> Chris Kapulkin
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+LeFanu+Lumsdaine"} Peter LeFanu Lumsdaine
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Voevodsky"} Vladimir Voevodsky
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1203.2553"} arXiv:1203.2553
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Kapulkin"}> Chris Kapulkin
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+LeFanu+Lumsdaine"} Peter LeFanu Lumsdaine
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em The Simplicial Model of Univalent Foundations (after Voevodsky)
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1211.2851"} arXiv:1211.2851
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://doi.org/10.4171/jems/1050"} doi:10.4171/jems/1050
          %h3#joyal_model_structure_on_simplicial_sets Joyal model structure on simplicial sets
          %p
            For references on the
